&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clever is on a mission to connect every student to a world of learning. As the leading identity platform for education, more than 111,000 schools worldwide use Clever to power secure digital learning experiences. With Clever’s layered security solutions, schools can protect access and identities for all staff, teachers, and students. With a secure identity platform for schools and a network of leading application providers, Clever is committed to advancing education with technology that works for students everywhere. Clever, a Kahoot! company, has an office in San Francisco, CA, but you can visit us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clever.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;clever.com &lt;/a&gt;anytime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team &amp;amp; Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Classroom Experience team at Clever builds the digital gateway to the classroom. As the Engineering Manager, you will lead the team responsible for our most visible products, including the Clever Portal—the daily starting point for millions of students and teachers. We are hiring a leader to help us expand our reach from the classroom into new frontiers like browser extensions and beyond, including future explorations of resource access outside our core products. This is a high-impact leadership role where you will manage the execution of our most visible user-facing products, hire and develop world-class engineering talent, and ensure that our technical strategy continues to provide simple, secure access to learning for everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make an Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The problem you’ll solve:&lt;/strong&gt; You will lead the team that scales our primary classroom user interfaces, connecting users to their learning applications through interfaces that work for kindergarteners in the classroom, through to administrators in the central office, and ensuring that the experience remains robust, delightful, and lightning-fast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you’ll partner with:&lt;/strong&gt; You will be a key strategic partner to Product, Design, and Marketing to define our roadmap, while working alongside other Engineering Managers to drive organizational best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like:&lt;/strong&gt; Success is a high-performing, inclusive team that delivers reliable, business-critical software, meets 99.98%+ uptime targets, and fosters a culture of continuous mentorship and professional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key projects you’ll lead:&lt;/strong&gt; You will drive the execution of accessible UIs and next-generation APIs that drive expanded, simple, and secure access to learning applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience (Must-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; 3+ years of experience managing engineering teams, with a proven ability to build high-impact teams — mentoring and coaching engineers at all levels while holding a consistently high bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Foundation:&lt;/strong&gt; 5+ years of software development experience with strong fundamentals in full-stack architecture and system design, along with familiarity with how core authentication concepts extend to device-level login.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Development Tools: &lt;/strong&gt;Familiarity with leveraging AI coding tools (such as Claude Code or Cursor) to enhance development workflow, productivity, and code quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cultural Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; A commitment to &lt;strong&gt;understand and prioritize the Clever engineering culture&lt;/strong&gt; (see our blog post on&lt;a href=&quot;https://engineering.clever.com/2017/09/06/defining-clevers-engineering-culture/&quot;&gt; Defining Clever&#39;s Engineering Culture&lt;/a&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with operational change management and process improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent communication skills and the ability to manage distributed, remote teams while building alignment across cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusive Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; A deep commitment to building diverse and inclusive teams where every voice is heard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (Nice-to-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer-Facing Scale:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing teams that build products for millions of concurrent users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High Availability:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience managing business-critical services with strict uptime requirements (99.98%+).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with our core technologies, including &lt;strong&gt;Go, Node.js, TypeScript, and React&lt;/strong&gt;, managing services within the AWS Ecosystem, and native device technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible PTO and Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive health, vision, and dental coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental healthcare services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual company retreat + team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range of our base salary cash compensation for this role for candidates living in the United States, besides NYC and San Francisco, CA, is between&lt;strong&gt; $167,000 - $230,000&lt;/strong&gt;. For candidates living in NYC and San Francisco, CA, it’s between&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;$183,000 - $253,000.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;All final offers are determined using multiple factors, including experience and level of expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clever believes classrooms and our company should be diverse and inclusive. We celebrate actions that build diverse teams, include every voice, and create safe spaces for everyone to bring their authentic selves to work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clever does not conduct interviews via text or Telegram. We will never ask for your financial information or reimbursement of equipment of any kind. If you receive any communications regarding employment with Clever that you think might be a scam, please email &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;mailto:recruitingscam@clever.co&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;mailto:recruitingscam@clever.co&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;recruitingscam@clever.com.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a resident of Colorado, please note you have the right to redact your age-related information like age, birth date, or dates of schooling.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clever is on a mission to connect every student to a world of learning. As the leading identity platform for education, more than 111,000 schools worldwide use Clever to power secure digital learning experiences. With Clever’s layered security solutions, schools can protect access and identities for all staff, teachers, and students. With a secure identity platform for schools and a network of leading application providers, Clever is committed to advancing education with technology that works for students everywhere. Clever, a Kahoot! company, has an office in San Francisco, CA, but you can visit us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clever.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;clever.com &lt;/a&gt;anytime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team &amp;amp; Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Executive Administrator to serve as the primary executive support to our CEO and assist other members of Clever&#39;s Executive Leadership Team as needed. This is a high-impact, highly trusted role in a primarily remote environment, with occasional travel for key in-person meetings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Clever continues to grow and evolve, this person will help our CEO and leadership team stay organized, aligned, and prepared through moments of change. You&#39;ll bring structure to shifting priorities, help make communication smoother across stakeholders, and create the operational clarity leaders need to move work forward thoughtfully.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be someone who can read the room, even virtually; anticipate what the CEO and other leaders need; and keep priorities, calendars, travel, and logistics moving smoothly. You&#39;ll help reduce administrative friction, create clarity, and make sure our leaders are prepared for the moments that matter most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is a great fit for someone who is resourceful, detail-oriented, thrives in a fast-moving, collaborative environment, and is confident navigating competing priorities. If you enjoy solving problems before they become problems, building trust across multiple stakeholders, and helping a mission-driven organization run more effectively, we&#39;d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make an Impact:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work proactively to help the CEO operate at optimal capacity.&lt;/strong&gt; As primary support to our CEO, you&#39;ll manage complex calendars, resolve scheduling conflicts, coordinate travel, and clear administrative noise, while also extending support to other executives as capacity allows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide excellent remote-first executive support. &lt;/strong&gt;Most of your work will be done virtually, so you&#39;ll need to be proactive, responsive, and thoughtful in how you support leaders from afar. You&#39;ll know when to move quickly, when to ask the right questions, and when to make a judgment call.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support high-stakes leadership moments. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll help coordinate and prepare for Board meetings, executive offsites, and other key gatherings where details matter and the experience needs to feel seamless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner across teams. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with the CEO and other members of the Executive and Senior Leadership Team, as well as cross-functional stakeholders and board members, to ensure clear communication and well-organized logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create systems that help the team scale&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ll look for ways to make recurring processes smoother, from travel planning and meeting prep to Board materials and executive coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience (Must-Haves)&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extensive senior EA experience to a CEO: &lt;/strong&gt;You have 3–5 years of experience serving as a senior Executive Assistant to a CEO or business unit leader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong Executive communication: &lt;/strong&gt;You are a specialist in executive-level written and verbal communication, precise, polished, and able to adjust tone across different leaders and audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prioritization and organizational efficiency: &lt;/strong&gt;You excel at finding the signal through the noise, quickly assessing what&#39;s urgent, what can wait, and what needs escalation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calendar and travel expertise: &lt;/strong&gt;You are highly skilled at managing complex calendars for multiple leaders, across time zones, and amid competing priorities. You can quickly assess tradeoffs and make thoughtful recommendations when schedules collide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote environment:&lt;/strong&gt; You know how to provide high-quality executive support in a virtual environment, be highly available and responsive during working hours, and know when to move quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust and discretion: &lt;/strong&gt;Discretion and confidentiality are non-negotiable. Leaders can count on you to operate with professionalism and good judgment in both remote and in-person settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel flexibility: &lt;/strong&gt;You are willing and able to travel up to 20% for executive offsites, leadership gatherings, or other important in-person moments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (Nice-to-Haves)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global coordination: &lt;/strong&gt;You can effectively coordinate across international time zones as Clever’s footprint continues to grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event and offsite planning: &lt;/strong&gt;You have experience planning leadership offsites, board meetings, and executive meetings where logistics, preparation, and experience all matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-forward:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience using AI tools to work smarter and improve efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion &amp;amp; Belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Clever believes classrooms and our company should be diverse and inclusive. We celebrate actions that build diverse teams, include every voice, and create safe spaces for everyone to bring their authentic selves to work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CLEVER BENEFITS AND PERKS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A competitive salary&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Paid Parental Leave&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Top-notch healthcare, vision, and dental coverage for you and your family&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Best-in-class mental healthcare service that supports employees&#39; mental and emotional wellness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A generous personal development yearly budget which can be used for courses, conferences, trainings, books, and more&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A comprehensive Learning &amp;amp; Development program that enables employees to enhance their skills, knowledge, and functional expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Annual company and team events to connect with fun, bright coworkers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The range of our base salary cash compensation for this role for candidates living in the United States, besides NYC and San Francisco, CA, is between&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;102,000&lt;/span&gt; and $120,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;For candidates living in NYC and San Francisco, CA, the salary is between&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;$112,000 and $132,000&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;All final offers are determined using multiple factors, including experience and level of expertise.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTICE OF ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE USE IN HIRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that Clever Inc. (“Clever”) uses artificial intelligence (AI) tools as part of our hiring process for certain positions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Systems Used:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willo.ai &lt;/strong&gt;(developed by Willo) - Used for candidate assessments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BrightHire Screen &lt;/strong&gt;(developed by BrightHire) - Used for initial phone screening&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Granola.ai&lt;/strong&gt; (developed by Granola) - Used for AI-powered transcription and note-taking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment Decisions Affected:&lt;/strong&gt; Recruitment and hiring&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose and Data Collected:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The assessment tool evaluates candidate responses to [e.g., skills questions, situational judgment scenarios] and generates scores that are reviewed by human recruiters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The conversational bot conducts initial phone screenings, collecting candidate responses to preliminary qualification questions, which are then reviewed by human recruiters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The AI Note-Taking tool allows our interviewers to focus entirely on our conversation rather than manual typing. These transcripts are used solely for internal evaluation and are handled in accordance with our data privacy policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Review:&lt;/strong&gt; All AI-generated outputs are reviewed by human decision-makers before any hiring decisions are made.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contact:&lt;/strong&gt; For questions about our use of AI in hiring, contact our Talent Acquisition Team at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:ta-ai-transparency@clever.com&quot;&gt;ta-ai-transparency@clever.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodation Requests:&lt;/strong&gt; If you require a reasonable accommodation related to our use of AI tools or if you are applying from a jurisdiction which gives you specific rights to opt out of AI review and you would like to use that right, please contact our Talent Acquisition Team at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:ta-ai-transparency@clever.com&quot;&gt;ta-ai-transparency@clever.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to request an alternative assessment process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Discrimination Statement:&lt;/strong&gt; Clever does not use AI for any employment decision that has the effect of subjecting employees or applicants to discrimination on the basis of any class protected under the Illinois Human Rights Act, nor do we use zip codes as a proxy for protected classes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clever does not conduct interviews via text or Telegram. We will never ask for your financial information or reimbursement of equipment of any kind. If you receive any communications regarding employment with Clever that you think might be a scam, please email &lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;mailto:recruitingscam@clever.co&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;mailto:recruitingscam@clever.co&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;recruitingscam@clever.com.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;If you are a resident of Colorado, please note you have the right to redact your age-related information like age, birth date, or dates of schooling.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Clever is on a mission to connect every student to a world of learning. As the leading identity platform for education, more than 111,000 schools worldwide use Clever to power secure digital learning experiences. With Clever’s layered security solutions, schools can protect access and identities for all staff, teachers, and students. With a secure identity platform for schools and a network of leading application providers, Clever is committed to advancing education with technology that works for students everywhere. Clever, a Kahoot! company, has an office in San Francisco, CA, but you can visit us at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.clever.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;clever.com &lt;/a&gt;anytime.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team &amp;amp; Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The District Dashboard team is responsible for the &quot;front door&quot; experience for our School Organization Administrators. As a Senior Product Designer on this team, you’ll be the design lead for the most critical interface in our ecosystem—the place where administrators manage digital learning for entire districts. You’ll join a high-performing &quot;quad&quot; (Product Manager, Engineering Manager, and Product Marketing Manager) to solve complex architectural challenges. Because many teams at Clever build features within this dashboard, you will act as the primary steward of the user experience, ensuring that every new addition fits into a cohesive, intuitive whole.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make an Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Problem You’ll Solve:&lt;/strong&gt; You will oversee the &quot;birds-eye view&quot; of the School Organization Dashboard, evolving a scalable information architecture as we introduce new features. You will tackle foundational challenges like reimagining Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and strengthening app governance and compliance frameworks. You will also be the primary owner of our design system, Dewey--maintaining, delegating tasks, and leading its AI-powered evolution in close partnership with Engineering. Additionally, you will lead the charge in remediating accessibility issues to ensure our tools are inclusive for all administrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You’ll Partner With:&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll work in close collaboration with your dedicated quad (Product Designer, Product Manager, Engineering Manager, Product Marketing Manager) and serve as a bridge between various product teams to ensure design consistency across the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like:&lt;/strong&gt; Success means maintaining a high bar for craft while scaling our design system. You will also be a key visionary, exploring how to evolve the School Organization Dashboard with value-add AI solutions that could fundamentally change how our product works in the long term.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Projects You’ll Lead:&lt;/strong&gt; You will lead the &quot;Long Term Vision&quot; for the dashboard with high-level prototyping of AI-driven troubleshooting workflows that help School Organization Admins minimize digital learning disruptions. You’ll also manage the roadmap for our design system evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience (Must-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;Significant experience in product design, specifically managing complex information architecture and B2B/Enterprise workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Systems Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience maintaining and evolving design systems, including the ability to delegate design tasks and collaborate with Engineering on implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong User Research Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable leading discovery, conducting interviews, and translating user insights into architectural changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tooling &amp;amp; Prototyping:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct experience using AI tools for design and development, specifically including prototyping with Claude Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accessibility Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; A deep understanding of WCAG standards and experience remediating accessibility issues in complex web products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (Nice-to-Haves):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in the EdTech space or building products for school administrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with Cybersecurity products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a &quot;quad&quot; model (Product Designer, Product Manager, Engineering Manager, Product Marketing Manager).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The range of our base salary cash compensation for this role for candidates living in the United States, besides NYC and San Francisco, CA, is between &lt;strong&gt;$149,000-$175,000&lt;/strong&gt;. For candidates living in NYC and San Francisco, CA, it&#39;s between&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;$165,000-$192,000&lt;/strong&gt;. All final offers are determined using multiple factors, including experience and level of expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
